--TEST--
`implements Iterator<int> by $field;` synthesizes the same forward a plain interface gets, and the forwarded class drives a `foreach` — `rule:classes/delegation-by-field`, `rule:iteration/concrete-generic-implements`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// The forward is written against the *interface's* signature, and a
// compiler-owned generic's signature still names its type variables — nothing
// substitutes them, because there is no call site here to substitute them
// against. So `current(): T` is a parameter slot whose type is unconstrained,
// and the forward declares it at the representation every unconstrained
// position already has (`nvs_ir::lower::erase_checked_ty`).
class Walker implements Iterator<int> {
    public int $i;
    public array<int> $items;

    public function constructor(array<int> $items) {
        $this->items = $items;
        $this->i = -1;
    }

    public function advance(): bool {
        $this->i = $this->i + 1;
        return $this->i < Core\Arr::count($this->items) as int;
    }

    public function current(): int {
        return $this->items[$this->i];
    }
}

final class Wrapped implements Iterator<int> by $inner {
    private Iterator<int> $inner;

    public function constructor(Iterator<int> $inner) {
        $this->inner = $inner;
    }
}

array<int> $xs = [7, 8, 9];

// Driven by hand, the way `rule:iteration/two-interfaces`' protocol is written.
Wrapped $w = new Wrapped(new Walker($xs));
while ($w->advance()) {
    echo $w->current(), "\n";
}

// And through the interface-typed read, which is the half a call-site rewrite
// could not answer: the forward has to be a row in `Wrapped`'s own method
// table for this to dispatch at all.
Iterator<int> $it = new Wrapped(new Walker($xs));
int $sum = 0;
foreach ($it as int $each) {
    $sum = $sum + $each;
}
echo "sum=", $sum, "\n";

// The agreement the shape asks for rather than a fourth line read off the
// output: the delegate and the forward must answer the same sequence, so a
// forward that erased a variable to something the delegate does not return
// fails this while still printing plausible numbers above.
Walker $bare = new Walker($xs);
Wrapped $forwarded = new Wrapped(new Walker($xs));
int $agreed = 0;
while ($bare->advance()) {
    $forwarded->advance();
    if ($bare->current() == $forwarded->current()) { $agreed = $agreed + 1; }
}
echo "agreed=", $agreed, "/3\n";
--EXPECT--
7
8
9
sum=24
agreed=3/3
